<title>NEW ZEALAND: CanWest buys NZ More FM's 8 radio stations.</title>
<headline>CanWest buys NZ More FM's 8 radio stations.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The private owners of eight New Zealand major market radio stations belonging to the More FM network said on Monday they had sold the business to Canada's CanWest Global Communications.</p>
<p>No financial details were given in a statement that said founding partners Doug Gold and Craig Thomson would continue in their senior management roles.</p>
<p>CanWest is the major owner of New Zealand's TV3, the main competitor in national television broadcasting.  </p>
<p>More FM's network is the second largest after that of The Radio Network (formerly Radio New Zealand).</p>
<p>The sale to CanWest is subject to regulatory consents.</p>
<p>--Wellington newsroom +64 4 471 4273</p>
